# Confidence gate (D-46/D-47 — pre-edit)

**Dan standing preference (D-47):** **"I want the 97% rule to be followed with every edit."** Before **every file edit** (product code, verify scripts, rules, docs, PROJECT_STATUS — any repo write), reach **conf ≥ 97%** first: classify → raise conf (scouts/reads/focused Dan question) → then edit. Solution Verifier PASS/N/A per D-36/D-43 applies on its own triggers **in addition**; 97% does not replace Solution Verifier when D-36 requires it. Platform parity automatic (D-32).

## When it applies

**Every file edit** — no path-class or substantive-only carve-out for the confidence bar. Runs **after** announce-and-go classification (`model-gates.mdc`), **before the first edit** in any task (including Phase 1 in `composer-grok-collab.mdc`).

## Sequence

1. **Classify** — `PROJECT_STATUS/MODEL_DOSSIER.md` + agent-ops skill → archetype, tier, cheapest model, **confStart** (state in reply). **Classify alone may yield ≥97%** for unambiguous T0 edits, typos, or docs-only clarifications with an explicit fix list — no scout fan-out required when classification already locks files, acceptance, and approach.
2. **If conf < 97%** — **no edits** (any path): parallel scouts / targeted reads; lock root cause, files, acceptance; one focused Dan question when UX/scope is ambiguous; for substantive product work also **Grok Solution Verifier** until agreed (D-36/D-43 Phase 1).
3. **Edit only when** conf ≥ 97%. Substantive product work **also** requires `solution-verifier:` PASS or N/A (D-36 skip reasons unchanged) **before the first edit in scope** (D-48 — not after implement, not deferred to parent). **`solution-verifier: N/A` and away items with approved approach-level specs do not skip the conf bar** — they skip Phase 1 Solution Verifier only; conf ≥ 97% still required before the first edit.
4. **Session log** — record archetype, model, conf as it rises (completion report or brain `outcomes/*.jsonl` per `agent-ops.mdc`).

## Scope persistence

Once conf ≥ 97% for the **current task scope**, that confidence **holds for subsequent edits in the same scope** until scope materially widens, acceptance becomes ambiguous, or a failed verify/build drops conf below 97% — then re-raise before the next edit.

## Skips (confidence bar only — tiny)

- **Default: none.** Misclassifying down to skip the bar = failure mode.
- **Mechanical version bump** — `package.json` `version` field only, in the **same ship commit** as work already completed at conf ≥ 97%, with no other semantic change in that hunk.

Planning/Q&A/repair loops run their own verifiers; they do **not** exempt reaching 97% before editing files in those loops.

## Solution Verifier ordering (D-48)

When D-36 requires **Solution Verifier**, **PASS** (or a valid **N/A** reason per `model-gates.mdc`) must be **evidenced in-session before the first edit** in that scope — **together with** conf ≥ 97%, not instead of it.

- **Workers/subagents:** MUST NOT implement product/code and defer Solution Verifier to the parent. Parent completes Phase 1 (Agree) **before** dispatching implementation, **or** the worker dispatches readonly Solution Verifier and reaches PASS/N/A **before** its first edit.
- **Forbidden:** edit-first then Solution Verifier; "parent will verify later"; completion-report-only `solution-verifier:` after diffs already exist.
- **Missing when triggered** = **NOT RUN** — do not ship or declare done.

## Relation

Does not replace D-36/D-43 (Solution Verifier, Build Checker, UI Playwright, Ship Verifier). **D-47** widens D-46: the **97% floor binds every edit**; **D-48** locks Solution Verifier **before first edit** when D-36 applies.
